                <pb facs="0771" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-22T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 22,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 22—6:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>453. Your 356, December 4, 3 p.m. Minister of Finance formally states that
                    Chinese American Bank of Commerce has already been instructed to remit interest
                    in full.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
